73bd91eaf8869e6ad1df774c6eb739c8d71ccf19cddd47ec4959c7b5fbdcdca7,"Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 25 Stormwater management

Clause # 2.25 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): The flow of stormwater from developments needs to be managed so as to negate or reduce to an acceptable frequency the possibility of flooding buildings and/or the danger to life at any location, through the storage of stormwater where appropriate in developments and the control of major development drainage systems.

Clause # 2.25.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To protect the urban environment from the effects of otherwise uncontrolled surface stormwater flows resulting from infrequent (and lesser) storm events.

Clause # 2.25.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To minimise or negate disruption and/or danger to both pedestrian and vehicular traffic that may be caused by otherwise uncontrolled surface stormwater flows resulting from frequent storm events.

Clause # 2.25.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To protect the quality of receiving waters, adjacent and downstream land-use and the rights of adjacent and downstream landowners.

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): On Site Detention	Yes (3, 6)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): On Site Retention	Yes (3,8)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): Gravity Pipe System Required	Yes (4)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): Pump System Permitted	No (4)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): Drainage Easement over downstream property (2)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): Qualified Engineer required to prepare drainage design	Yes (3, 6)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (environmental_protection): Sediment Control Plan Required	Yes (1)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): Positive Covenant Required (i.e. Section88E (3) Instrument)	No (5)

Clause 2.25.3.1 - other (development_control): Where easements are necessary over any adjoining or downstream property to achieve gravity drainage, a written agreement from the adjoining owners is to be submitted with the SDCP.

Clause 2.25.3.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Development activities must not cause an adverse impact on adjoining or any other properties. This includes preserving surface flow paths and not increasing water levels.

Clause 2.25.3.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Site discharges will need to be restricted to pre-development discharges using On-site Stormwater Detention (OSD) and On Site Retention (OSR).

Clause 2.25.3.3 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): OSD or OSR of stormwater is required to limit discharges from developments to pre-development conditions.

Clause 2.25.3.3 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): For developments greater than $1 0 0 0 { \mathfrak { m } } ^ ",Text
c2f8da61953d8020633e31395a6f836f394d9f10310b5b7f51e86e407480fd7f,"{ 2 }$ in site area, allowable discharges will be limited to the equivalent fully pervious discharges for the site area.

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): Extensions (alterations and additions) where the proposed extended roof or paved area are less than $4 0 \mathsf { m } ^ { 2 }$ .

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): Sites that discharge directly to the Cooks River or into a major Sydney Water Corporation controlled trunk drainage system

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): For single dwelling developments, where a maximum of two residential dwellings are being created (including secondary dwellings, alterations and additions, dual occupancies, attached and semi-detached), on-site retention (OSR) may be used in lieu of OSD.

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): The OSR system must adhere to the following:

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): Lot size (sqm)	OSR tank size per lot (Strata or Torrens Title) (Litres)
Greater than 200	Minimum 5,000
Less than 200 but greater than 100	Minimum 4,000
Less than 100	Minimum 3,000

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): The OSR must provide water to all new and/or upgraded toilet cisterns, laundry washing machine connections, external taps and irrigation systems. Standard labelling shall be displayed at such outlets.

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): OSR is not required as per the same exclusions applying to OSD under C5 i and ii above.

Clause 2.25.3.3 - other (development_control): For other developments excluded by the above, OSR may be used to offset the calculated OSD storage volume at a rate of $1 \mathsf { m } ^ { 3 }$, for every $2 . 5 \mathsf { m } ^ { 3 }$ of OSR storage provided (up to a maximum OSD offset of $1 0 \mathsf { m } ^ { 3 } \big ]$ ).

